  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Key and API usage",
      "items": [
        "The API key lives in page memory and clears on reload. (js/state.js:2–4; js/setup.js:49–64; README.md:27–31)",
        "The browser sends it directly to api.anthropic.com; usage may incur charges on the player's Anthropic account. (js/api.js:7–16; README.md:29–31)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Turn and retry behavior",
      "items": [
        "Only one request runs at a time. The action enters conversation history after a successful response; on failure it returns to the input for retry. (js/adventure.js:3–13; js/adventure.js:45–88)",
        "Requests time out after 60 seconds; HTTP errors, unreadable responses, and empty text responses become errors for the turn flow. (js/api.js:3–6; js/api.js:18–44)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Response-controlled stats",
      "items": [
        "Stat tags apply in response order. Health stays from 0 through max health and gold cannot fall below 0; attack and defense have no clamp in this code. (js/stats.js:1–15)",
        "At zero health, the page shows the end message and disables further actions. (js/stats.js:17–25; js/adventure.js:3–13)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Tests and CI",
      "items": [
        "The Node suite uses node:test, vm, and mocked DOM and fetch behavior. (tests/functionality.test.cjs:1–5; tests/functionality.test.cjs:241–294)",
        "The GitHub workflow builds with jekyll/builder on pushes and pull requests to main. This workflow contains no test invocation or deployment step. (.github/workflows/jekyll-docker.yml:1–19)"
      ]
    }
  ]
